EASSYBUY — COMPLETE SHOPPING APPLICATION API ROADMAP
=====================================================
Base URL: /api
Project: Spring Boot + MySQL
Purpose: Buyer, Seller, Admin, Super Admin APIs, with real-time shopping features.

IMPORTANT DESIGN RULES
----------------------
1. These are endpoint designs/recommendations, not proof that every endpoint already exists in the code.
2. Use REST APIs for normal create/read/update/delete operations. Use Server-Sent Events (SSE) or WebSocket only where the client benefits from live updates.
3. Do not create duplicate endpoints for the same business action. In this roadmap, checkout is the normal way to create a buyer order; do not separately expose POST /api/orders unless you intentionally support another validated order-creation flow.
4. The logged-in user identity must come from the authenticated JWT/security context, not from a userId supplied by the client.
5. Enforce ownership and role checks for every buyer, seller, admin, and super-admin endpoint.
6. Use database transactions and atomic stock updates for checkout/inventory. Payment webhooks must be signature-verified and idempotent.
7. SSE is one-way server-to-client. Use WebSocket only if the client and server both need to send frequent live messages.
8. Use pagination/filtering for large lists. Validate input and return consistent error responses.

