=====================================================
PART 17 — SECURITY AND TEST CHECKLIST
=====================================================

- Buyer A cannot view or modify Buyer B's cart, address, order, payment, notification, or wishlist.
- Seller A cannot view or update Seller B's products/orders.
- Only approved/active sellers can publish products.
- Only authorized Admins can approve/reject sellers and products.
- Only SUPER_ADMIN can manage admin accounts and high-privilege roles.
- Product prices, discounts, delivery fees, and totals are recalculated on the server.
- Inventory decrement/reservation is atomic under concurrent checkout.
- Expired reservations are released safely and only once.
- Duplicate checkout/payment requests do not create duplicate orders or charges.
- Payment/shipping webhooks verify signatures and handle duplicate events.
- Order state transitions reject invalid actions.
- Refunds are tied to valid orders/payments and audited.
- SSE connections are authenticated, authorized, rate-limited where appropriate, and cleaned up.
- DTO validation, pagination limits, rate limiting, and global exception handling are implemented.
- Secrets, tokens, payment data, personal documents, and stack traces are never exposed in logs or error responses.

